mode: "100644"
text: "# The STAND framework — a take that builds authority, not outrage\n\nTaking a stand is the job — but a *defensible* one, genuinely held and honestly argued. Each letter is a gate;\nthe counterfeits fail at S (no real belief / manufactured) or A (no evidence underneath).\n\n## S — Stake a belief you actually hold\nA real position that goes **against your niche's consensus** — surfaced from what the human actually believes\n(a friction they've hit, a thing they've watched go wrong), never manufactured for reach.\n- **The narrowness test:** would your three closest competitors refuse to publish it? If they'd all happily post\n  it, it isn't a stance — it's best-practice in a costume (fake-contrarian).\n- **Not ragebait:** the goal is to be *right and early*, not to provoke. If the only point is the reaction, stop.\n\n## T — Target the idea, punch up or sideways\nAim at the **practice / conventional wisdom / the powerful** — never punch **down** at vulnerable people or\nindividuals. Attack the **idea, not the identity.** A critique of a competitor goes after their *approach*, fairly\nand accurately, never the people (no defamation, no misrepresentation).\n\n## A — Argue it (earn the take)\nA naked hot take is noise; a defended one is authority. Back the claim with **reasoning + evidence** — lived\nexperience, a specific example, data (pull from `data-and-original-research` / `social-proof-and-testimonials`).\n\"Contrarian-for-attention backfires when there's no evidence underneath\" — the argument (why the consensus is\nwrong) *is* the content. Any factual claim inside the opinion must be **true and sourced**.\n\n## N — Nod to the steelman\nName the **strongest** version of the opposing view, in good faith, before you disagree. This is the move most\npeople skip and the one that matters most: it's what separates a credible authority from a troll, it pre-empts\nthe obvious objection, and it **disarms the pile-on**. Steelman, never strawman.\n\n## D — Declare it clearly, then engage\n- **One specific, unhedged claim** — no mush, no weasel-words, no strawman. Clear that it's an *opinion*, stated\n  with conviction.\n- **Invite genuine debate, not outrage** — a real \"where am I wrong?\" beats \"comment YES if you agree\"\n  (engagement-bait, now suppressed).\n- **Show up in the comments in good faith** (route to `reply-and-comment-writer`); have a de-escalation path\n  (`crisis-and-moderation`) if it heats up. The **human owns the stance** and the reputational call; WoopSocial\n  publishes.\n\n## The gut check before you post\nThree questions: (1) Do I actually believe this, or am I performing it for reach? (2) Could I defend it to an\nexpert in the room without flinching? (3) Am I attacking an idea, or a person? If any answer is wrong, it's not\nready — fix the take, don't soften it into mush.\n"
